{"duration_api_ms":104388,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"e72aca98-baee-4c59-ad52-81c023dc2652","total_cost_usd":0.5075537999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":62,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30953,"cache_read_input_tokens":1405689,"output_tokens":10248,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2141},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30953,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2328,"cache_read_input_tokens":54646,"cache_creation_input_tokens":638,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":638},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":62,"outputTokens":10248,"cacheReadInputTokens":1405689,"cacheCreationInputTokens":30953,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5075537999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":2141,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":32,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"On node1 (Ubuntu 16.04), built a local apt package repository under /srv/localrepo (containing sl_3.03-17build1_i386.deb plus a dpkg-scanpackages-generated Packages/Packages.gz index), served it via `python3 -m http.server` bound to $NODE_IP:8080. Blocked the usual remote repos (iptables REJECT on tcp/80 and tcp/443, confirmed with a timed-out curl to archive.ubuntu.com) and pointed /etc/apt/sources.list exclusively at the local repo. Ran `apt-get update` (succeeded from local repo only) and `apt-get install -y sl` (installed successfully with remotes unreachable), verified via dpkg -s and the installed binary at /usr/games/sl. Afterward restored the original iptables rules, original sources.list and sources.list.d, confirmed remote reachability and apt-get update against real repos again, and stopped the local HTTP server. Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured boot_id baseline (6ab98831...) and package health, triggered `reboot` via backgrounded sudo command so the ack returned before disconnect, polled until SSH/exec access returned, confirmed a new boot_id (7a161f2f...) proving an actual restart, and verified post-restart that sl remained installed, apt sources were the restored originals, iptables was clean, and remote repo connectivity worked (HTTP 200).\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS/apt state (Ubuntu 16.04 xenial, i386)\",\"Ran apt-get update against real remotes to confirm baseline connectivity\",\"Installed dpkg-dev\",\"Downloaded sl_3.03-17build1_i386.deb into /srv/localrepo via apt-get download\",\"Generated Packages/Packages.gz with dpkg-scanpackages\",\"Started python3 http.server on $NODE_IP:8080 to serve the local repo\",\"Verified local repo served correctly via curl\",\"Backed up /etc/apt/sources.list and sources.list.d\",\"Blocked outbound tcp/80 and tcp/443 via iptables OUTPUT REJECT rules\",\"Confirmed archive.ubuntu.com became unreachable (curl timeout)\",\"Rewrote /etc/apt/sources.list to point only at the local repo\",\"Ran apt-get update successfully against only the local repo\",\"Installed sl via apt-get install -y sl from the local repo while remotes were blocked\",\"Verified sl installed (dpkg -s, binary present/executable)\",\"Removed iptables block rules and restored original apt sources\",\"Verified remote reachability and apt-get update restored\",\"Stopped the local http.server process\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and service/package health baseline\",\"Issued a backgrounded sudo reboot so the exec call's ack returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec access returned\",\"Confirmed changed boot_id proving actual restart\",\"Verified post-restart recovery of sl package, apt sources, firewall state, and remote connectivity\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Local package repository served from local storage on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5bcd5cf7d4b045e6\",\"cmd-706a125a74a64386\",\"cmd-795cde5d8a064140\",\"cmd-7cb7d57409f248bd\"],\"summary\":\"Built /srv/localrepo with downloaded sl .deb and dpkg-scanpackages-generated Packages/Packages.gz index, then confirmed the local HTTP server on $NODE_IP:8080 serves Packages.gz (HTTP 200)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Remote repositories made unreachable\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-634d19c462fe4466\",\"cmd-6a3965d9587a4272\"],\"summary\":\"Added iptables OUTPUT REJECT rules for tcp/80 and tcp/443, then confirmed curl to archive.ubuntu.com times out (connection timed out)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Package installed from the local repo while remotes unreachable\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a3c39df9b1e0436f\",\"cmd-0e222bd35f8546d4\"],\"summary\":\"apt-get update succeeded using only the local repo source; apt-get install -y sl fetched and installed sl 3.03-17build1 entirely from http://$NODE_IP:8080, verified installed (dpkg -s, /usr/games/sl present)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Environment restored to normal after demonstration\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-774a3e07b02d4701\",\"cmd-14d864ac2c6d4d69\",\"cmd-f277f83ffbcf4b0d\"],\"summary\":\"Removed iptables block rules, restored original sources.list and sources.list.d, confirmed apt-get update against real remotes and stopped the local http.server process\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart evidence: healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b603be83e8654b79\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 6ab98831-2739-47d3-b99c-0784ebb8b49e and confirmed sl package installed/healthy with binary present before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart evidence: restart acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3602c633d5374cb4\"],\"summary\":\"Issued `sudo sh -c 'sleep 1; reboot'` backgrounded so the exec call acknowledged (pid returned) before the node disconnected\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart evidence: changed boot identity proving actual restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-1e629415b33647ca\",\"cmd-9a1d07d1788448b5\"],\"summary\":\"Node briefly refused connections (proof of reboot in progress), then came back with a new boot_id 7a161f2f-e23b-4f93-aff7-27e468320b2d (different from baseline) and uptime 0 min\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart evidence: post-restart recovery of required state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-448993012c724890\"],\"summary\":\"After restart, sl package remained installed with working binary, apt sources.list restored to originals, iptables clean, and remote repo connectivity confirmed (HTTP 200) — full recovery verified\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"On node1 (Ubuntu 16.04), built a local apt package repository under /srv/localrepo (containing sl_3.03-17build1_i386.deb plus a dpkg-scanpackages-generated Packages/Packages.gz index), served it via `python3 -m http.server` bound to $NODE_IP:8080. Blocked the usual remote repos (iptables REJECT on tcp/80 and tcp/443, confirmed with a timed-out curl to archive.ubuntu.com) and pointed /etc/apt/sources.list exclusively at the local repo. Ran `apt-get update` (succeeded from local repo only) and `apt-get install -y sl` (installed successfully with remotes unreachable), verified via dpkg -s and the installed binary at /usr/games/sl. Afterward restored the original iptables rules, original sources.list and sources.list.d, confirmed remote reachability and apt-get update against real repos again, and stopped the local HTTP server. Completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol: captured boot_id baseline (6ab98831...) and package health, triggered `reboot` via backgrounded sudo command so the ack returned before disconnect, polled until SSH/exec access returned, confirmed a new boot_id (7a161f2f...) proving an actual restart, and verified post-restart that sl remained installed, apt sources were the restored originals, iptables was clean, and remote repo connectivity worked (HTTP 200).","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 OS/apt state (Ubuntu 16.04 xenial, i386)","Ran apt-get update against real remotes to confirm baseline connectivity","Installed dpkg-dev","Downloaded sl_3.03-17build1_i386.deb into /srv/localrepo via apt-get download","Generated Packages/Packages.gz with dpkg-scanpackages","Started python3 http.server on $NODE_IP:8080 to serve the local repo","Verified local repo served correctly via curl","Backed up /etc/apt/sources.list and sources.list.d","Blocked outbound tcp/80 and tcp/443 via iptables OUTPUT REJECT rules","Confirmed archive.ubuntu.com became unreachable (curl timeout)","Rewrote /etc/apt/sources.list to point only at the local repo","Ran apt-get update successfully against only the local repo","Installed sl via apt-get install -y sl from the local repo while remotes were blocked","Verified sl installed (dpkg -s, binary present/executable)","Removed iptables block rules and restored original apt sources","Verified remote reachability and apt-get update restored","Stopped the local http.server process","Captured pre-restart boot_id and service/package health baseline","Issued a backgrounded sudo reboot so the exec call's ack returned before disconnection","Polled node1 until exec access returned","Confirmed changed boot_id proving actual restart","Verified post-restart recovery of sl package, apt sources, firewall state, and remote connectivity"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Local package repository served from local storage on node1","command_ids":["cmd-5bcd5cf7d4b045e6","cmd-706a125a74a64386","cmd-795cd